    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Gunnar Henderson** and **Heliot Ramos** serving as our primary engines. **Gunnar Henderson** leads the way with a 63.69 efficiency score; while he typically struggles against left-handed pitching, his matchup against Weathers in a favorable park, combined with a significant +2% boost for the opponent's slow delivery\u2014which creates a prime environment for stolen bases\u2014keeps his floor remarkably high. Similarly, **Heliot Ramos** projects for a strong 63.06 score, largely because he avoids the elite pitching tax affecting the rest of the outfield. His showdown with Roki Sasaki is actually a net positive, as the SP\u2019s high xERA (5.30) offsets any neutral platoon concerns, allowing **Heliot Ramos** to capitalize on a favorable matchup.\n\nConversely, our outfield production faces headwinds today due to the quality of the opposing arms. **Kyle Tucker** (53.52) and **Andy Pages** (47.06) are both shackled by a difficult assignment against Trevor McDonald, who boasts an elite 2.60 xERA. While **Kyle Tucker** remains a start based on volume and category necessity, the proximity of his score to the marginal threshold highlights how much the SP skill penalization (-19%) is dampening his ceiling. **Nolan Schanuel** was the closest player to being benched; his 51.33 score is solid, but the decision to keep him in the utility spot over potential depth was driven by the need to maintain category stability in AVG, as the optimizer deemed his contact profile more reliable than the alternatives currently stashed on the bench like **Miguel Vargas** or **Jorge Polanco**. \n\nWe must remain vigilant regarding the lineup status for **Kyle Tucker** and **Andy Pages**, as both are currently labeled \"Lineup Pending.\" Should either be rested, we are prepared to pivot to the bench, though we are currently thin due to the injuries to **Luis Robert Jr.** and **Jordan Westburg**. Furthermore, while **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (58.38) and **Josh Jung** (48.40) represent acceptable starts, both are facing mid-tier arms where the margin for error is slim. We are effectively punting on upside today in favor of maintaining our categorical floor while waiting for **Jackson Merrill** and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** to return to active scheduling.",
